{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/math\/customdimensions"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety"],"anchor":"Extending-the-Framework","title":"Extending the Framework","generated":true}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Custom Dimensions and Units","modules":[{"name":"Math"}]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CustomDimensions","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Math","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ships with a comprehensive set of base dimensions (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/length"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/time"},{"text":", and friends) and derived dimensions (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/speed"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/energy"},{"text":", and more). These cover physics and everyday measurement, but your app almost certainly measures things that aren’t in the SI system too: money, hit points, ingredients, resource points, users, and so on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The good news: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension"},{"text":" is an open system. Because a dimension is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"just a dictionary of exponent powers"}]},{"text":", you can describe any dimension you can imagine at runtime.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Define a Custom Dimension","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Define-a-Custom-Dimension"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Create a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension"},{"text":" with a dictionary of exponent identifiers. Each key is a dimension name and each value is its power:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Math","","\/\/ A dimension for money, with a single base exponent.","let usdDimension = PhysicalDimension(exponents: [\"USD\": 1])","","\/\/ A dimension for \"users\", used later in per-user metrics.","let userDimension = PhysicalDimension(exponents: [\"user\": 1])"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can build compound custom dimensions with the same arithmetic used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"internally: ","type":"text"},{"code":"+","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" multiplies dimensions, "},{"code":"-","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" divides them, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"*"},{"type":"text","text":" with an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" raises a dimension to a power:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let revenuePerUser = usdDimension - userDimension   \/\/ [\"USD\": 1, \"user\": -1]"]},{"level":3,"text":"Define Custom Units","anchor":"Define-Custom-Units","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Custom dimensions don’t have a compile-time type, so use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/unknown","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" as the type-level parameter and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/NamedUnit","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"create units. Pass a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/LinearConverter"},{"text":" (for a simple scale) or an","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/OffsetConverter"},{"text":" (for a scale plus an offset) to handle conversions:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let usdUnit = NamedUnit<MathDimension.unknown>(","    symbol: \"$\",","    dimension: usdDimension,","    converter: LinearConverter(coefficient: 1.0)",")","","\/\/ EUR is defined relative to the same base dimension.","let eurUnit = NamedUnit<MathDimension.unknown>(","    symbol: \"€\",","    dimension: usdDimension,","    converter: LinearConverter(coefficient: 1.09)",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"name":"Tip","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Keep the same ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PhysicalDimension"},{"type":"text","text":" value (here "},{"code":"usdDimension","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") for every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unit in a family. The framework only converts between units whose dimensions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"match, so sharing the exact same value makes your money interchangeable."}]}],"style":"tip","type":"aside"},{"level":3,"text":"Convert Between Custom Units","anchor":"Convert-Between-Custom-Units","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Custom units convert exactly like the built-in ones:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let walletInEur = Quantity(value: 100.0, unit: eurUnit)","let walletInUsd = walletInEur.converted(to: usdUnit)","","print(walletInUsd.value) \/\/ 109.0"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Combine Custom Units with Built-In Ones","anchor":"Combine-Custom-Units-with-Built-In-Ones","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Custom dimensions participate in dimensional arithmetic too. Here a currency","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dimension combines with the built-in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/time"},{"text":" dimension:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let hourlyRate = Quantity(value: 50.0, unit: usdUnit) \/ Quantity(value: 1.0, unit: Units.hour)","","print(hourlyRate.value)          \/\/ 50.0","print(hourlyRate.unit.dimension) \/\/ [\"USD\": 1, \"time\": -1]","print(hourlyRate.unit.symbol)    \/\/ \"($\/h)\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Use the Currency Dimension","anchor":"Use-the-Currency-Dimension","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If your custom dimension happens to be currency, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Math"},{"text":" already defines a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/currency"},{"text":" dimension and a built-in library of world","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"currencies (and cryptocurrencies) in ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units"},{"text":". Currency units automatically","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"place their symbol before the value when formatting:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let gift = Quantity(value: 100.0, unit: Units.usd)","print(gift.formatted()) \/\/ \"$100.00\"","","\/\/ Resolve units from ISO 4217 codes at runtime.","if let currency = Units.currency(for: \"SEK\") {","    print(currency.symbol) \/\/ \"kr\"","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"What’s Next?","anchor":"Whats-Next","type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to lock custom units into a compile-time dimension in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explore "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units"},{"type":"text","text":" to see the breadth of units provided out of the box."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Extend ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Math"},{"text":" with your own physical dimensions and units—currency, points, gameplay metrics, or anything else your app measures.","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math"]]},"references":{"doc://Math/documentation/Math/UnitConverter":{"type":"topic","title":"UnitConverter","url":"\/documentation\/math\/unitconverter","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UnitConverter"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UnitConverter"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/UnitConverter","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that converts numeric values between a unit and the base unit of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension."}]},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/PhysicalDimension/length":{"url":"\/documentation\/math\/physicaldimension\/length","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The dimension of length (SI base unit: meter).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"length"},{"kind":"text","text":": `Self`"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/length","title":"length"},"doc://Math/documentation/Mat